  "strategy": "# 1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe core idea is to improve upon the parent solution (47-point step function) for the minimum overlap integral problem by:\n1. Using a piecewise constant function representation with variable resolution (n_points)\n2. Optimizing over n_points choices (notably powers of 2 for efficient computation)\n3. Employing both global search (BOBYA) and local optimization for robustness\n4. Using directed search starting from the parent solution\n\nThe algorithm addresses:\n- Non-convexity through basin hopping\n- High dimensionality (n_points) through function parameterization\n- Budget constraints with iterative scaling and restart\n\nIts basis is evolutionary optimization (BOBYA) combined with local acceleration and parent-initialization.",
